<%# Two states, because the keys do nothing until focus is in the grid. Which
    one shows is decided in CSS off .keyboard-mode on the grid itself, so the
    controller never has to reach outside its own element.

    Both halves are one short line: the toolbar row's height is set by the
    --control-size select beside it, and a legend taller than that would move
    the grid every time the two swap.

    The keys themselves live in the ? dialog now. Reciting them here meant two
    copies of the same list, and only one of them could be complete — ⌥S is a
    page shortcut, not a grid one. %>
<div class="keyboard-legend">
  <p class="keyboard-legend-enter"><kbd>Tab</kbd> to enter keyboard mode</p>

  <%# The grid points aria-describedby here, so this is read on the way in. %>
  <p id="start_page_keys" class="keyboard-legend-keys"><kbd>?</kbd> for all the shortcuts</p>
</div>
